# Repo-wide line-ending policy (see version-fox/vfox#727).
#
# Baseline: let git decide which files are text. Text is stored with LF in the
# repository and follows the machine's core.autocrlf/core.eol on checkout;
# binaries (shim.exe, test.zip, images) are detected and never converted.
# Do not replace this with a blanket `* text` or `* text eol=lf`, which would
# disable binary detection and corrupt those files.
* text=auto

# Everything below must be LF in every working tree, whatever core.autocrlf or
# core.eol a machine uses. `eol=lf` overrides both on checkout.

# Scripts that a shell executes or sources. A trailing CR breaks every command
# ("$'\r': command not found") and the shebang line (the interpreter becomes
# "pwsh\r"), and the completions are packaged as-is by goreleaser (archives,
# brew, deb/rpm).
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
completions/** text eol=lf

# Go toolchain files. gofmt always emits LF and reports CRLF sources as
# unformatted; the go command writes go.mod/go.sum with LF, and
# `go mod tidy -diff` reports a CRLF go.sum.
*.go text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf

# Checksum manifests read by `sha256sum -c`/`shasum -c`. Some verifiers keep the
# CR as part of the file name and then cannot find "shim.exe".
*.sha256 text eol=lf
*.sha512 text eol=lf
